1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,610
The Marriage of Figaro, episode eight: the trap in the garden.

2
00:00:03,930 --> 00:00:08,220
The Count paces. A locked closet, a letter, a jump from a window. Is he being played?

3
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:17,970
The Countess has a new plan, and this one she keeps even from Figaro. Susanna will promise the Count a meeting in the garden tonight, but the Countess herself will go, in Susanna's clothes.

4
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:28,110
Susanna finds the Count. Will she come? Yes, she says, if he gives her the dowry he promised, so she can pay off Marcellina. Their duet is Crudel, perché finora: cruel girl, why make me wait so long?

5
00:00:28,430 --> 00:00:32,780
He is delighted. But leaving, Susanna whispers to Figaro: you've already won your case.

6
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:34,680
The Count hears it. A trap!

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,140
In Vedrò mentr'io sospiro he rages: shall I sigh while my servant is happy? Never. Figaro will marry Marcellina.

8
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:44,130
And the judge, Don Curzio, is ready with the verdict.

9
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:45,920
Next episode: Mother!
